Look at the dog! It is small. It is cute. It is our dog, Bidu. You are my new classmate. Are you from Brazil? Yes, you are. You are very nice. They are my parents, Mr. and Mrs. Souza. They are very kind. They are on vacation.

We are all together now. I am very happy. You are my friend. He is a good teacher. She is a great doctor. It is a beautiful day. We are one big family. They are our neighbors. Goodbye!', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Tom é um homem. Em inglês, usamos o pronome ''he'' (ele) para homens. O texto diz: ''He is a teacher.''","options":["She","He","It","You"],"prompt":"What pronoun do we use for Tom?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Maria é uma mulher. Usamos o pronome ''she'' (ela) para mulheres. O texto diz: ''She is a doctor.''","options":["He","She","It","They"],"prompt":"What pronoun do we use for Maria?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Para animais e coisas, usamos o pronome ''it'' (ele/ela, neutro). O texto diz: ''It is small.''","options":["He","She","It","We"],"prompt":"What pronoun do we use for the dog?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
